                  <provenance type="#s c"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_444">Pershore,
                        Worcestershire. Benedictine abbey of St Edburga (originally of St Mary the
                        Virgin, St Peter, and St Paul). </orgName><p>Table of contents in same hand
                        as St John's Coll. 96.</p><p>'pershor' scribbled in a late medieval hand in
                        the upper margin of fol. 23*r (the last leaf of the De doctrina
                        christiana).</p><p>The contents include the account of the translation of
                        Edburga's relics to Pershore and her miracles there.</p><p>Sir John Prise
                        (no. 40 in the list of his books in the Jesus register). Later at Jesus
                        where Twine saw it.</p></provenance>
